WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.990
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.360
Mr. Penguin's Broken Heart

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.630
Here ya go.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.450
I didn't order this.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.150
These pancakes are a new menu item.

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:48.310
Try them out.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.090
There's no bamboo grass in it.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.400
There usually wouldn't be.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.050
It's a little salty.

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:03.550
I tried putting salmon in it.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.320
You should try it, too, Miss Sasako.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.900
Oh, sure.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.270
It is a little salty.

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:18.210
Oh, when did you get here, Mr. Penguin?

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:19.750
I've been here the whole time!

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:24.570
I noticed, but I wasn't sure 
if I should talk to you.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.640
Talk to me!

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.920
Would you like some salmon pancakes?

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.830
I don't feel like eating right now.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.180
What's the matter?

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:38.760
Can't you tell by looking?

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.090
Nope.

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:44.500
My... my...

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:50.520
My heart's been broken!

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.230
Broken heart <i>(shitsuren)</i>?

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.360
That would be a portable 
charcoal stove <i>(shichirin)</i>.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.080
That would be a unicycle <i>(ichirinsha)</i>!

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:03.950
That would be a tricycle <i>(sanrinsha)</i>!

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.220
My heart is broken,

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:08.020
so I don't have the energy to retort!

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.060
You just did.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.240
Did Miss Penko break your heart?

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.920
Who else would it be?

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:17.090
Um, I don't know what to say.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.490
Don't say anything.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.050
Just leave me alone.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:27.470
I hear that the bagel shop in front 
of the station is pretty good, Panda.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.440
Really?

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.020
Listen to me!

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.690
You want us to listen?

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.270
Of course!

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.090
You'll feel better if you talk.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.240
Officer, I...

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.700
Hey! I'm not a criminal!

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.650
So, what happened?

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:47.220
I saw it.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:47.910
What?

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:51.280
Miss Penko was on a date.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.580
W-With who?

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.050
Well, surprisingly...

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.380
Yeah?

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.830
It's someone you'd never expect...

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:03.680
Yes?

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:07.060
I still can't believe it...

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.140
Who was it?

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:12.500
You would never expect it...

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:16.690
Hurry up and spit it out!

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.230
I told you, I'm not a criminal!

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:22.740
I saw them earlier at the park.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:28.660
Oh!

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.510
Miss Penko!

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:37.040
What a chance encounter 
to see her here.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.190
It's fate!

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.390
Well, this is unexpected Miss—

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:54.900
Sorry... to... keep... you... waiting.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.630
Well, let's go.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.940
Really? Mr. Tortoise?

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.460
Wow, really?

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:06.740
It was Mr. Tortoise?

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:12.160
That's right. 
They met up and went for a date.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.700
What a wonderful café.

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:23.090
I... come here... to sunbathe.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:24.760
Oh, my.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:32.830
I want... some, too...

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:33.930
Here you go.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.940
What a beautiful day.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.160
It is....

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.530
They were totally enjoying 
having tea at the café,

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:45.720
and she was feeding him,

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.510
and they were on a boat together!

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.520
Where were you hearing all of this?

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:53.410
Well...

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:07.270
That's somehow touching.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:12.260
But I don't think any of those 
things mean they're going out.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.970
But then something happened 
to make it official...

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:21.690
I really like turtles...

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:33.080
It can't be!

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:40.040
I had no idea that 
Miss Penko liked turtles.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.590
What's so good about turtles?

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:45.950
I'm asking you, 
what's so good about them?

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.760
Tell me the truth!

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.720
M-Maybe because they have a shell?

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.430
The fact that their head and 
legs scrunch in might be cute.

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:58.390
It's amazing that they live 
for a thousand years.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.350
Penguins have amazing qualities, too!

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:05.890
We don't?!

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:10.290
I've lost. I've completely lost.

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:13.280
Why was I born a penguin?

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:18.560
Mom, why didn't you give 
birth to me as a turtle?

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.790
Mr. Penguin, you know,

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:23.250
penguins don't give 
birth to turtles.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.350
I know that!

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:27.530
Aw man, if I knew this 
was going to happen...

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.450
I should have just asked Miss 
Penko out for a drive.

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:32.280
I-I don't think it's too late.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:33.220
Huh?

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.510
You did just get your license...

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.800
Y-You're right!

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:42.300
But if Miss Penko likes turtles, 
she might not like fast things.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:47.180
So it has to be slow?!

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:48.900
It's no use.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:52.400
I'm going to give up on 
Miss Penko completely.

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:55.150
That might be for the better.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:55.620
Yup.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.530
You'll find another nice girl.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:02.630
You're right, I've got to move on.

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:03.330
Yup.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:05.660
You're right.

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:10.300
I shouldn't give up that easily!

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.080
Which is it?

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.750
But Miss Penko has Mr. Tortoise.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:18.440
There's no way I'm going 
to lose to a tortoise!

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:25.300
Oh, Mr. Tortoise.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:30.510
Good... after...noon.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.600
Your rival is here.

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.770
Miss Penko's boyfriend is here.

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:37.080
Don't say that.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:39.110
Are you going to duel now?

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:40.250
No, they're not.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:45.850
Um, I think they call this shabadaba.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:47.280
You mean a clash of titans <i>(shuraba)</i>.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.360
Hey, shut up for a second!

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:54.320
Anyways, I have to find out 
what he's doing with

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:55.840
Miss Penko once and for all.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.400
T-Tortoise.

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.980
What?

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:03.310
Well, um...

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:05.570
What a nice day.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:10.240
Weren't you going to find out 
what he's doing, Mr. Penguin?

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:12.030
I know that!

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:17.270
Is something... wrong?

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:20.870
Um, well... I-I was wondering, 
at the park the other day...

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:25.320
I ate a really delicious sardine.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:26.920
It was so good.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.460
That's not it.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:30.750
I know that!

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:32.840
There's a certain order in conversations!

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:40.360
Oh yeah, at the park, you were 
with a girl penguin, right?

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:45.170
It's such a nice park.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:47.550
So, what's the relationship 
between you and

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:49.020
Miss Penko, Mr. Tortoise?

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.370
Don't be so blunt about it!

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.990
So why were you two together?

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.240
You, too, Miss Sasako?!

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:58.200
Why were you two together at the park?

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:03.160
I was... invited...

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:07.120
Miss Penko invited you?

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:10.580
She said that she likes....

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:14.760
...turtles <i>(kame)</i>...

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:23.660
May you two live happily together!

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.800
...ra...

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:30.800
Ra?

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:38.980
Wait a second.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:41.810
If Miss Penko likes turtles so much...

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.580
Welcome.

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:59.570
Good... after...noon...

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:03.640
What are you doing, Mr. Penguin?

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:07.350
Where did you get that shell?

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:10.390
It's hard.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:17.020
Miss Penko... really likes... turtles....

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:18.240
Oh, about that...

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:25.400
What Miss Penko really likes 
are cameras, not turtles (kame).

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.330
Kame 
Turtle

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.330
ra

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:26.700
Kamera 
Camera

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:29.160
Huh?

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:32.230
Apparently she's really 
into cameras as of late.

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:34.380
Mr. Tortoise apparently 
has the same hobby.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:38.340
What she really likes are 
cameras, not turtles.

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:48.670
I'm gonna start over.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:57.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:56.780
Panda's Night Out.

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:01.140
Thanks for all of your hard work.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:03.940
Thank you.

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:09.990
We're closed now, Panda.

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.150
Panda?

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:17.080
Oh, good morning.

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:18.410
It's already night time.

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:22.530
Grizzly.

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:26.300
Hey, let's go play for a bit.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:28.190
Sure.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:30.080
You're gonna go play?

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.730
I wanna go, too!

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:34.840
We ain't goin' anywhere for kids.

00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:37.170
This is an adult's night out.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.230
Night out?

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:41.520
That sounds really fun.

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.820
Why the hell are you tagging along?

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:51.180
Because you invited me, Grizzly.

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:52.830
Not you.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:55.800
Him!

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:57.290
Where are you going?

00:12:58.030 --> 00:13:00.800
So, Panda,

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:02.300
I regret to inform you,

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:04.840
tonight's plans have been canceled 
and we're going home.

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.160
How sad.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:07.890
How the hell did it come to that?!

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:09.310
Wait a minute!

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:10.510
So you are going?

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:12.930
Of course I am!

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:22.820
Wow! What is this place?

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:25.110
It's a batting center.

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.570
You've never been to one?

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:29.920
What the hell are you doing?!

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:32.970
This isn't a place you're supposed 
to be climbing around!

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:34.400
Really?

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:36.540
Jeez...

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:42.730
This feels really good.

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:44.470
That's not what those are used for.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:49.660
This does work quite well 
to relieve tension.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:52.390
What the hell are you 
doing it for, too?!

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:55.200
So what are we supposed to do here?

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:58.100
You hit the ball that comes at you.

00:13:58.580 --> 00:13:59.960
Like this.

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:04.740
Home Run

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:07.450
Nice catch!

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:10.320
You're amazing, Polar Bear!

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:11.510
It was a line drive at the pitcher.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.730
What the hell are you doing?!

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:15.330
I wanna do it, too!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.960
You don't have to!

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.170
Nice shot!

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:25.950
You did it, Mr. Grizzly!

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:28.680
I don't feel like doing this anymore.

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:31.300
Then I'll show you how it's done.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.220
Bring it on!

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:34.930
You're holding too many bats!

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.890
Let's try this again.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:41.400
Use the damn bat!

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:45.360
Enough. Just try it, Panda.

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:50.620
Raise your bat and 
watch the ball carefully, Panda.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:51.240
Okay!

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:59.610
That's not what we meant.

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:01.750
Watch the ball closely.

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:04.780
Stare...

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:05.810
Like this?

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:07.080
Hit the ball.

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:08.700
I thought so.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:11.140
Not "I thought so." 
Hit the damn ball with the bat!

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:14.800
Nice shot!

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:15.910
Yay!

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:17.520
This isn't golf!

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:20.230
They aren't building blocks!

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:23.690
This isn't billiards!

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:32.950
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:35.880
That was fun.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:38.730
You didn't bat at all, though.

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.170
We're going to the next place.

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:42.020
We're going somewhere else?

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:43.880
The night's just beginning.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:46.380
It's just beginning...

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:48.980
I wonder where we're going next!

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:52.050
B
a
t
h
 
E
